  "timeoriginalestimate": null,
  "description": {
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1,
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "What happens now",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Two small things about the three Work In Progress filters do not match the written description."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "One: each filter offers its Clear action all the time, even before anything has been picked. The description asks for it to appear only once at least one thing is selected. It is also labelled \"Clear all\" where the description calls it a single \"Clear\" action."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Two: the Customer and Asset filters each have an \"All customers\" / \"All assets\" item pinned at the top of their list, but the Advisor filter has no \"All advisors\" item at all - its list starts with \"Clear all\" and then the advisors. The closed control does read \"All advisors\", so the state exists; it is the item that is missing."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "How to see it",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Open Reports, then Work In Progress, without touching any filter."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Open the Customer filter: the list reads \"All customers\", \"Clear all\", then the customers - and nothing is selected yet. The Asset filter behaves the same way."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Open the Advisor filter: the list reads \"Clear all\", then Admin ShopView. There is no \"All advisors\" item."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "What should happen instead",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The Clear action should appear only once something is selected, and the Advisor filter should offer an \"All advisors\" item like the other two."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "What we tested it on",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "QA branch sv8582, build v3.5-16cf83f, on 6 August 2026. Date range This Week, both locations, nothing selected in any filter."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "How bad is it",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Low. Everything still works - Clear all does return the filter to its all state, and the closed control shows the right words. It is only when each control appears that differs."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "What we ruled out",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "We checked the useful half first: each filter does list the values found across the whole scope, the closed labels do read \"All advisors\", \"All customers\" and \"All assets\", and Clear all does put the filter back."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Where this expected behaviour comes from",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Work In Progress report specification, version 9, requirement S7-R3, which says: \"When no customer is selected, the Customer filter reads \"All customers\" and every job is shown; the filter offers a single \"Clear\" action that returns it to \"All customers\", shown only once at least one customer is selected.\"."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Work In Progress report specification, version 9, requirement S7-R5, which says: \"When no asset is selected, the Asset filter reads \"All assets\" and every job is shown; the filter offers a single \"Clear\" action that returns it to \"All assets\", shown only once at least one asset is selected.\"."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The Advisor filter half rests on S7-R1, which describes the Advisor filter as the same kind of multi-select as the other two."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "That is source type 2: the specification (PRD) in Confluence. The version number given is the Confluence page version, not the version written inside the page."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
